{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QsrXh1YcsVbCYE3THt6k2j","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now I have all the information needed to provide a comprehensive summary. Let me compile the findings:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've found the exact patterns you need. Here's what you're looking for:\n\n### DiffTest Struct Fields (from pkg/testutils/difftest.go)\n\nThe `DiffTest` struct has these fields:\n- **Name** (string): Identifies the subtest (used with t.Run)\n- **Args** ([]string): Command-line arguments passed to both binaries\n- **Stdin** ([]byte): Input to stdin; nil means EOF immediately, empty non-nil slice also produces no bytes but represents an open stdin that closes\n- **Env** ([]string): Environment variables; nil inherits test process env with LC_ALL=C; non-nil KEY=VALUE pairs are merged into inherited env\n- **WorkDir** (string): Working directory for the test; defaults to t.TempDir() when empty\n- **ExitCode** (int): Expected exit code; defaults to 0 when zero value\n- **Normalize** ([]NormalizeFunc): Slice of normalization functions applied in order to stdout and stderr before comparison\n- **ExpectedFiles** (map[string][]byte): Map of expected file paths to their contents\n\n### Representative Test Files with Error Cases\n\n**File: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5200/cmd/head/head_test.go`**\n\nThis is an excellent full example with error test cases:\n\n```go\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\npackage main\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"os/exec\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"testing\"\n\n\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils\"\n)\n\nfunc TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n\tgoBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n\trefBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"ghead\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Skip(\"reference binary not found\")\n\t}\n\n\tdiscardStderr := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func([]byte) []byte { return nil })\n\n\ttests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n\t\t// R4.4: default 10 lines (no flags)\n\t\t{\n\t\t\tName:  \"default-10-lines\",\n\t\t\tStdin: seq(1, 20),\n\t\t},\n\t\t// ... other success cases ...\n\t\t// Error: invalid byte count\n\t\t{\n\t\t\tName:      \"bytes-invalid\",\n\t\t\tArgs:      []string{\"-c\", \"abc\"},\n\t\t\tExitCode:  1,\n\t\t\tNormalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStderr},\n\t\t},\n\t}\n\ttestutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n}\n\nfunc TestDiffHeaders(t *testing.T) {\n\tgoBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n\trefBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"ghead\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Skip(\"reference binary not found\")\n\t}\n\n\tdir := t.TempDir()\n\twriteFixture(t, dir, \"a.txt\", \"alpha\\nbravo\\ncharlie\\n\")\n\twriteFixture(t, dir, \"b.txt\", \"delta\\necho\\nfoxtrot\\n\")\n\n\tdiscardStderr := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func([]byte) []byte { return nil })\n\n\ttests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n\t\t// ... success cases ...\n\t\t// R3.5: error on non-existent file continues processing\n\t\t{\n\t\t\tName:      \"nonexistent-with-valid\",\n\t\t\tArgs:      []string{\"nonexistent.txt\", \"a.txt\"},\n\t\t\tWorkDir:   dir,\n\t\t\tExitCode:  1,\n\t\t\tNormalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStderr},\n\t\t},\n\t\t// R3.5+R4.2: valid file then nonexistent\n\t\t{\n\t\t\tName:      \"valid-then-nonexistent\",\n\t\t\tArgs:      []string{\"a.txt\", \"nonexistent.txt\"},\n\t\t\tWorkDir:   dir,\n\t\t\tExitCode:  1,\n\t\t\tNormalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStderr},\n\t\t},\n\t\t// R3.5+R4.2: nonexistent between valid files\n\t\t{\n\t\t\tName:      \"nonexistent-between-valid\",\n\t\t\tArgs:      []string{\"a.txt\", \"nonexistent.txt\", \"b.txt\"},\n\t\t\tWorkDir:   dir,\n\t\t\tExitCode:  1,\n\t\t\tNormalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStderr},\n\t\t},\n\t\t// R4.2: single nonexistent file\n\t\t{\n\t\t\tName:      \"nonexistent-only\",\n\t\t\tArgs:      []string{\"nonexistent.txt\"},\n\t\t\tWorkDir:   dir,\n\t\t\tExitCode:  1,\n\t\t\tNormalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStderr},\n\t\t},\n\t}\n\ttestutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n}\n\nfunc writeFixture(t *testing.T, dir, name, content string) {\n\tt.Helper()\n\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(dir, name), []byte(content), 0o644); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc bytes512() []byte {\n\tb := make([]byte, 600)\n\tfor i := range b {\n\t\tb[i] = byte('a' + i%26)\n\t}\n\treturn b\n}\n\nfunc seq(start, end int) []byte {\n\tvar b []byte\n\tfor i := start; i <= end; i++ {\n\t\tb = fmt.Appendf(b, \"%d\\n\", i)\n\t}\n\treturn b\n}\n```\n\n**File: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5200/cmd/seq/seq_test.go`**\n\nThis file shows error validation patterns well:\n\n```go\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\npackage main\n\nimport (\n\t\"os/exec\"\n\t\"regexp\"\n\t\"testing\"\n\n\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils\"\n)\n\nfunc TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n\tgoBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n\trefBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gseq\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Skip(\"reference binary not found\")\n\t}\n\n\tdiscardStdout := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func([]byte) []byte { return nil })\n\n\tbinaryNameRe := regexp.MustCompile(`(?:/\\S+/)?g?seq`)\n\tnormalizeBinaryName := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func(b []byte) []byte {\n\t\treturn binaryNameRe.ReplaceAll(b, []byte(\"seq\"))\n\t})\n\n\ttests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n\t\t// R4.2: non-numeric argument\n\t\t{\n\t\t\tName:      \"error-non-numeric\",\n\t\t\tArgs:      []string{\"abc\"},\n\t\t\tExitCode:  1,\n\t\t\tNormalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{normalizeBinaryName},\n\t\t},\n\t\t// R4.2: missing operand\n\t\t{\n\t\t\tName:      \"error-no-args\",\n\t\t\tExitCode:  1,\n\t\t\tNormalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{normalizeBinaryName},\n\t\t},\n\t\t// R4.2: extra operand\n\t\t{\n\t\t\tName:      \"error-extra-operand\",\n\t\t\tArgs:      []string{\"1\", \"2\", \"3\", \"4\"},\n\t\t\tExitCode:  1,\n\t\t\tNormalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{normalizeBinaryName},\n\t\t},\n\t\t// R4.2: zero step\n\t\t{\n\t\t\tName:      \"error-zero-step\",\n\t\t\tArgs:      []string{\"1\", \"0\", \"10\"},\n\t\t\tExitCode:  1,\n\t\t\tNormalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{normalizeBinaryName},\n\t\t},\n\t\t// R4.2: NaN argument\n\t\t{\n\t\t\tName:      \"error-nan\",\n\t\t\tArgs:      []string{\"nan\"},\n\t\t\tExitCode:  1,\n\t\t\tNormalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{normalizeBinaryName},\n\t\t},\n\t\t// R4.1: successful sequence exits 0\n\t\t{\n\t\t\tName: \"success-single-arg\",\n\t\t\tArgs: []string{\"3\"},\n\t\t},\n\t\t// ... more success cases ...\n\t}\n\ttestutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n}\n```\n\n### Key Patterns for Error Test Cases (Exit Code 1)\n\n1. **Basic error test structure:**\n   ```go\n   {\n       Name:      \"error-name\",\n       Args:      []string{\"invalid-args\"},\n       ExitCode:  1,\n       Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{normalizeFunctionName},\n   }\n   ```\n\n2. **Common normalizers for error cases:**\n   - `discardStderr` - when error messages differ between implementations\n   - `discardStdout` - for help/version output that differs\n   - `normalizeBinaryName` - to handle path differences in error messages\n\n3. **Files with WorkDir for error testing:**\n   ```go\n   {\n       Name:      \"error-nonexistent-file\",\n       Args:      []string{\"nonexistent.txt\"},\n       WorkDir:   dir,\n       ExitCode:  1,\n       Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{discardStderr},\n   }\n   ```\n\n4. **Test function setup:**\n   ```go\n   func TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n       goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n       refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"g<command>\")\n       if err != nil {\n           t.Skip(\"reference binary not found\")\n       }\n       // normalizer definitions\n       tests := []testutils.DiffTest{...}\n       testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refB